-- Seed the real `persons` catalog table from lib/mockData/persons.ts.
-- All rows are pre-vetted content (bios, filmography etc. live in code for
-- now — see mockData's own header), so they're inserted as status =
-- 'approved' directly, matching how portraits (0004) already skip a
-- moderation queue for the same reason. Run as the SQL editor / postgres
-- role, which bypasses RLS, same as every other migration here.
--
-- Idempotent: re-running only inserts rows for new slugs.
--
-- Review before running; this is not applied automatically.

on conflict (slug) do nothing;
